            "review_title": "Review at BBQ Plan-K",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nWorth it, always fresh from Vina Fresh Meat supply. Crowded, so go early!\nSep 2020\nThey are owned by Vina Fresh Meat butchery+supermarket chain, so they have a truly consistent supply of truly fresh meat, unlike at most other BBQ chains which have to serve you defrosted pork since it is cheaper for restaurants to buy frozen pork in bulk. You can choose the exact plate of meat that you want from their display refrigerator, and they will look exactly the same (with grammage and price info sticker displayed clearly on each plate of meat) if you were to get it from their Vina Fresh Meat supermarket. I must say, their good knowledge of pork, the right handling, is really much better than most of the local butchers. And they also have premium meats such as Iberico pork and wagyu, once again, at supermarket prices so they are really quite worth it, even for the premium meats.\n\nTheir menu is rather cute too, with a pictorial translation of some commonly used words in the restaurant to Korean-English-Vietnamese, so you'll know what to say to the servers if you want a certain item. Side dish (\"pan-chan\") includes the comforting Korean warm stew egg and authentic Korean spicy seafood soup, surprisingly with an entire flower crab!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 15, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
